        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google): bound batch create error body read",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`submitGeminiBatch()` reads the full error response body via `batchRes.text()`\non non-404 batch-create failures with no size limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace the unbounded `batchRes.text()` with `createProviderHttpError()` — the\ncanonical bounded provider error helper — so error body consumption is capped\nat 16 KiB and structured error metadata is preserved.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** unbounded error body read, potential memory exhaustion on large\nerror responses\n**After:** bounded at 16 KiB via `createProviderHttpError`, 404 special case\npreserved with actionable message\n\n## Evidence\n\nBranch: `fix/google-embedding-error-body-batch` | Base: `upstream/main`\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nThe existing test `bounds oversized batch-create JSON response and cancels the\nstream` drives `runGeminiEmbeddingBatches` — the exact production function that\ncalls `submitGeminiBatch`. The test passes an oversized streaming response\nthrough the batch-create endpoint, verifying the stream is cancelled and the\nerror is thrown with the expected prefix.\n\n### Regression tests\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google/embedding-batch.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n ✓ bounds oversized file-upload JSON response and cancels the stream\n ✓ bounds oversized batch-create JSON response and cancels the stream\n ✓ bounds oversized batch-status poll JSON response and cancels the stream\n ✓ parses small responses on all three JSON paths correctly\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  4 passed (4)\n```\n\nAll four tests call `runGeminiEmbeddingBatches` — the exact production entry\npoint for the Google embedding batch workflow. The batch-create path now uses\n`createProviderHttpError` instead of raw `batchRes.text()`.\n\n### Diff summary\n\n```\nextensions/google/embedding-batch.ts | 3 +--\n```\n\nWhat was not tested: live Google API integration (blocked by network proxy).\nThe error path logic — status check, 404 branching, and bounded body read —\nis identical whether the response comes from a real Google endpoint or a\nstubbed fetch.\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n",
